  "query_preview": "..\nA minor, relatively dry trade-wind surge continues across the region.\nThe Guam and Saipan ASOS have reported sustained winds just below 20\nknots, with Guam reporting isolated gusts up to 25 knots. On Thursday\nnight into Friday, model guidance indicates a trade-wind trough \npassing south of the region, bringing scattered showers and isolated \nthunderstorms, mainly concentrated over Guam. This was reflected in \nthe forecast with a slight difference in shower chances between Guam \nand CNMI. Thunderstorm chances are more likely for Guam than the \nCNMI, but still included the latter in the forecast due to omega \nvalues and increased relative humidity in the Saipan model time \nheights. Gusts near heavier showers will be around 25 mph.\nConsidering ongoing drought concerns, conserving any upcoming \nrainfall should be a priority as the dry season approaches. Once the \ntrough passes around Friday night, isolated showers may return for \nthe rest of the forecast period.",
